From 9942c62e77883e3aa455b4fc74ba84bd466e889f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:02:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] doc: HTTP/2 serving, WebSockets over HTTP/2 and the dialer's
 offer

doc/http2.md (started with the build options, CVEs and limits) now
explains what is served over HTTP/2 and where (TLS listeners only; not
public listeners with -publicfallback; why there is no h2c or
prior-knowledge cleartext HTTP/2), that each stream goes through the
HTTP/1.1 request path with the same rules, the remaining differences from
HTTP/1.1 (no 100-continue, 413 and 431 per stream without closing the
connection, 405 for classic CONNECT), RFC 8441 WebSockets and their
refusals, the OpenSSL calls ALPN relies on (the same on 1.1.1 and 3.x;
only 3.x/4.x were used), and the fuzz target and benchmark tooling.

doc/p2p-websocket.md gets an "Over HTTP/2" section (server, dialer,
getpeerinfo, fallbacks, the inbound peer's path through the HTTP I/O
threads, Windows answering 501) and an updated threat model and TLS
fingerprint: the dialer's ALPN offer now matches Chrome's
"h2, http/1.1" in HTTP/2 builds, while GREASE, extension order, ECH and the
HTTP/2 connection's own SETTINGS still differ from a browser.

Documentation only.

Coordinator integration provenance (network403):
Resolve integration context by retaining the incoming purposeful change together with existing shared/native consumers; exact old/new patch and file inventory is retained in owner-adaptations.json. No authored purpose or removed downstream behavior restored.
Original scripted commands/hashes above are original-author provenance; modified parent/tool/catalog hashes are not claimed to reproduce this composition. Exact coordinator adaptation scripts and ordered tree proof are in composed403-network-metrics-delivery. Build/runtime/benchmarks NOT_RUN for this composition under user compile-first policy.

